   "text": {
    "L1": "India has many languages, arts and crafts. Its people still live together as one nation.",
    "L2": "This is unity in diversity: differences can enrich one shared nation.",
    "L3": "For example, Aakansha makes Aipan in Uttarakhand, while Priyaranjan makes Dhokra in Odisha.",
    "L4": "Chitra makes coconut shell craft in Kerala, and Balamurali makes Kondapalli toys in Andhra Pradesh.",
    "L5": "A process must be told in order. Use words such as first, then, after that and at last.",
    "L6": "First, clean the shell. Then, make it smooth; after that, shape it and fix a base.",
    "L7": "At last, polish the shell so it shines. Chitra polishes the shell and makes bowls from it.",
    "L8": "Dhokra also follows an order: make the figure, carve details, melt out the wax, and pour in brass.",
    "L9": "So diversity does not mean division. Different traditions can belong to one united India."
   },
